Testing the Auth Flow
Go to http://localhost:5173 — you should land on the Login screen (not the CRUD table).
Click "Register here," create an account.
Log in with that account — you should now see the Student Records table.
Refresh the page — you should stay logged in (this is what check_session.php is for).
Click Logout — you should be sent back to the login screen, and CRUD calls should now fail with 401 if you try them without logging in.
Common auth-specific issues
Login works but refresh logs you out → withCredentials: true missing from a request, or Access-Control-Allow-Origin is still set to * (cookies won't be sent cross-origin with a wildcard).
"session_start(): Session cannot be started" → make sure session_start() is the very first line, before any echo or whitespace/output.
401 on every CRUD call even when logged in → the browser isn't sending the session cookie; double check withCredentials: true is on every axios call, not just login.

This gives you the full flow an NC III practical exam usually expects: register → login → session-gated CRUD → logout, all built from scratch with plain PHP and React, no external auth libraries.
